Let word be "MCMXCIV".
Let n be the number of characters in word.
Let total start at 0.

For every i from 0 to n - 1:
    Let value start at 0.
    Let c be character i of word.
    If c is 73, set value to 1.
    If c is 86, set value to 5.
    If c is 88, set value to 10.
    If c is 76, set value to 50.
    If c is 67, set value to 100.
    If c is 68, set value to 500.
    If c is 77, set value to 1000.
    If i + 1 < n:
        Let next value start at 0.
        Let next c be character (i + 1) of word.
        If next c is 86, set next value to 5.
        If next c is 88, set next value to 10.
        If next c is 76, set next value to 50.
        If next c is 67, set next value to 100.
        If next c is 68, set next value to 500.
        If next c is 77, set next value to 1000.
        If value < next value:
            Set total to total - value.
        Otherwise:
            Set total to total + value.
    Otherwise:
        Set total to total + value.

Print total.
